Input: {"decision_time_ms": 1790373599999, "macro_contexts": {"D1": {"context": {"always_in": "long", "always_in_relevance": "medium", "breakout_mode": true, "confidence": "medium", "decision_time_ms": 1790294399999, "directional_pressure": "bull", "evidence_against": ["The strongest counterargument is that the trend keeps producing spiking highs that are not held: bar 86 reached 2771 with a 255.70-point upper tail and was followed by 27 sideways bars, and bar 117 now shows the same shape with high 2850 and close 2775.61 (74.39-point tail), so the current 'breakout' may be another overshoot rather than a durable spike.", "Trading-range behaviour dominates the window: bars 11-35, 50-83 and 87-113 are three multi-week ranges covering roughly 86 of 120 bars, so this market has repeatedly reverted to range after every strong leg, which weakens a trend-continuation label.", "The pullback is large relative to the leg: 216.69 points (~7.6%) from 2850 to 2633.31 in only three bars, and bar 119's low 2641.37 undercuts the low 2641.70 of the breakout bar 117, a sign that the spike's momentum is already being absorbed.", "The last 20 bars are only net +207 (bar 101 close 2479.28 to bar 120 close 2686.59) while containing both a new high 2850 and a deep dip to 2358.62 (bar 111), i.e., two-sided rather than one-directional pressure."], "evidence_for": ["Acceptance above a multi-week range: four consecutive closes (2612.02, 2632.98, 2642.90, 2775.61) above the 2557.46 top of the 27-bar bars 87-113 range, with a new window high at 2850 (bar 117).", "Swing progression is upward across the window: higher lows 1368.42 -> 1512.91 -> 1803.74 -> 2357.18 paired with higher highs 1944.39 -> 1974.46 -> 2771 -> 2850.", "The pullback after the breakout is being bought above the breakout level: bars 118-120 hold low 2633.31, and bar 120 closes 2686.59, 129 points above 2557.46 and in the upper 81% of its own 66.08 range.", "The 27-bar range (bars 87-113) resolved upward with follow-through bars 115 and 116 (closes 2632.98 and 2642.90) rather than immediately reversing, unlike the failed bar 61 (1974.46) and bar 107 (2680) probes inside earlier ranges."], "missing_information": [], "observations": ["Window covers 120 closed D1 bars from open 1779926400000 to the final close 1790294399999; window low is 1368.42 (bar 10, close 1780790399999) and window high is 2850 (bar 117, close 1789948800000), a 108% advance from low to high.", "Bars 6-10 are five consecutive lower closes (1859.02, 1813.04, 1731.00, 1581.32, 1568.55), breaking the bars 1-5 range of 1958.77-2042.37; bar 6 opens 2006.06 with high 2006.17 and closes 1859.02.", "Bar 10 prints the window low 1368.42 but closes 1568.55, a 200.13-point lower tail (87% of its 230.85 range) - a climactic reversal bar rather than a clean bear trend bar.", "Bars 11-35 are two-sided and overlapping between high 1845.09 (bar 19) and low 1512.91 (bar 30); bar 30's 1512.91 is a higher low versus 1368.42.", "Bars 36-49 rally from 1597.72 (bar 36 low) to 1944.39 (bar 49 high) with consecutive bull closes 1889.93 and 1917.02 (bars 48-49).", "Bars 50-83 form a 34-bar overlapping range between 1803.74 (bar 51 low) and 1974.46 (bar 61 high); bar 61 opens 1953.92, tags 1974.46 and closes 1891.41, and bars 73 and 80 have ranges of only 13.24 and 10.41 (doji cluster).", "Bars 84-86 are a bull spike: bar 84 opens 1916.51 with low 1905.63 and closes 2252.16; bar 86 prints high 2771 but closes 2515.30, leaving a 255.70-point upper tail.", "Bars 87-113 hold a 27-bar range between 2357.18 (bar 98 low) and 2557.46 (bar 92 high); bar 107 spikes to 2680 and closes 2514.72 back inside the range.", "Bars 114-117 close 2612.02, 2632.98, 2642.90 and 2775.61, all above the 2557.46 range high, and bar 117 reaches the new window high 2850.", "Bars 118-120 pull back from bar 118 high 2776.18 to bar 120 low 2633.31; bar 119's low 2641.37 undercuts bar 117's low 2641.70, and bar 120 closes 2686.59 (81% of its 66.08 range) still 129 points above the 2557.46 breakout level."], "phase": "breakout-spike", "primary_regime": "bull-trend", "role": "CONTEXT_ANALYST", "schema": "brooks.market-context.v2", "structures": [{"description": "Bear breakout of the bars 1-5 range 1958.77-2042.37, with five consecutive bear closes down to the 1368.42 low; bar 6 opens 2006.06 and closes 1859.02, bar 10 closes 1568.55.", "end_time_ms": 1780790399999, "kind": "breakout", "lower_boundary": "1368.42", "start_time_ms": 1780358400000, "upper_boundary": "2042.37"}, {"description": "Sell-climax reversal bar at the 1368.42 low: close 1568.55 with a 200.13-point lower tail, ending the bear spike and starting the basing process.", "end_time_ms": 1780790399999, "kind": "climax", "lower_boundary": "1368.42", "start_time_ms": 1780704000000, "upper_boundary": "1599.27"}, {"description": "Post-spike two-sided range with heavy overlap and alternating closes; high 1845.09 (bar 19), higher low 1512.91 (bar 30), roughly 1500-1850 area.", "end_time_ms": 1783036799999, "kind": "range", "lower_boundary": "1512.91", "start_time_ms": 1780790400000, "upper_boundary": "1845.09"}, {"description": "Bull leg from the 1597.72 low (bar 36) to the 1944.39 high (bar 49), continued by a pullback low of 1803.74 (bar 51).", "end_time_ms": 1784073599999, "kind": "swing", "lower_boundary": "1597.72", "start_time_ms": 1782950400000, "upper_boundary": "1944.39"}, {"description": "34-bar overlapping range between 1803.74 (bar 51 low) and 1974.46 (bar 61 high); the bar 61 probe above 1974.46 failed and closed 1891.41, and bars 73 and 80 are very small doji bars.", "end_time_ms": 1787097600000, "kind": "range", "lower_boundary": "1803.74", "start_time_ms": 1784160000000, "upper_boundary": "1974.46"}, {"description": "Bull spike out of the 1800-1975 range: bar 84 rises from 1916.51 to close 2252.16, and bar 86 spikes to 2771 before closing 2515.30 (buy climax with a 255.70-point upper tail).", "end_time_ms": 1787356799999, "kind": "breakout", "lower_boundary": "1905.63", "start_time_ms": 1787097600000, "upper_boundary": "2771"}, {"description": "27-bar range after the spike between 2357.18 (bar 98 low) and 2557.46 (bar 92 high); bar 107 overshoots to 2680 but closes 2514.72 back inside the range.", "end_time_ms": 1789689599999, "kind": "range", "lower_boundary": "2357.18", "start_time_ms": 1787356800000, "upper_boundary": "2557.46"}, {"description": "Four-bar breakout above the 2557.46 range top: closes 2612.02, 2632.98, 2642.90 and 2775.61, with bar 117 printing the window high 2850 (74.39-point upper tail).", "end_time_ms": 1789948800000, "kind": "breakout", "lower_boundary": "2436.87", "start_time_ms": 1789689600000, "upper_boundary": "2850"}, {"description": "Three-bar pullback from bar 118 high 2776.18 to bar 120 low 2633.31 that holds above the 2557.46 breakout level; bar 119's low 2641.37 undercuts bar 117's low 2641.70 and bar 120 closes 2686.59 near the top of its range.", "end_time_ms": 1790294399999, "kind": "swing", "lower_boundary": "2633.31", "start_time_ms": 1790035200000, "upper_boundary": "2776.18"}], "symbol": "ETH-USDT", "timeframe": "D1", "transition_conditions": ["Two or more consecutive closes above 2776.18 (bar 118 high) would confirm the bars 114-117 leg as a continuing spike and keep the read as bull breakout.", "A daily close back below 2557.46 (the bars 87-113 range top) would mark the breakout as failed and revert the primary read to trading-range with an upper boundary near 2850.", "A close below bar 120's low 2633.31 followed by a lower high below 2776.18 would shift the always-in to short and raise the higher-high MTR-like interpretation of 2771 versus 2850.", "Continued overlapping closes between roughly 2633 and 2776 with small bodies would move the phase from breakout-spike toward channel or range without changing the bullish regime label."], "window_bars": 120}, "freshness": "current"}, "H4": {"context": {"always_in": "unclear", "always_in_relevance": "low", "breakout_mode": true, "confidence": "medium", "decision_time_ms": 1790366399999, "directional_pressure": "balanced", "evidence_against": ["26 bars since the 2850 high are two-sided - 12 bars inside 2716.01-2804.59 and 13 bars inside 2633.31-2740.42 - and 2804.59 is a lower high versus 2850, so the market is in a range, not an advancing bull trend.", "Bar 94 closed at 2723.15 with a 126.75 upper tail after a 191.94 range, a possible buy climax rather than a measured-move breakout; no bar has closed above 2804.59 since.", "The last decisive breakout was bearish: bar 107 closed at 2659.00 below the 2716.01 low, and the current range floor 2633.31 is below that broken range, a step down.", "Repeated 2696.09-2699.53 highs in bars 114/116/119 plus inside bars and shrinking ranges (17.82 in bar 120) show neither side gaining acceptance, so Always-In is two-sided."], "evidence_for": ["Swing structure stays bullish: rising lows 2358.62 (bar 60), 2568.16 (bar 88), 2633.31 (bar 112) and highs 2700.00 (bars 82/92) then 2850 (bar 94); no bull swing low has been broken.", "The 2358.62-2850 leg gained 20.8% in 34 bars and the pullback low 2633.31 holds far above the old range top 2528.80, so the earlier breakout was accepted rather than reversed.", "Bar 107's break below 2716.01 got no follow-through: bar 108 closed at 2676.47 near its high (2676-2681 range) and price moved back into 2660-2716 for 12 more bars.", "The 2850-to-2633.31 pullback is about 44% of the prior leg, a common bull-flag depth, and bar 120 closed at 2692.59 in the upper quarter of its range."], "missing_information": [], "observations": ["120 closed H4 bars from 1788638400000 (close 1788652799999) to 1790352000000 (close 1790366399999); window high 2850 (bar 94, 1789977600000), window low 2358.62 (bar 60, 1789488000000).", "Last close 2692.59 sits in the upper quarter of bar 120's 2678.27-2696.09 range; bars 114/116/119 topped at 2699.39/2699.53/2696.09 without a close above 2700.", "Bar 94: open 2658.81, high 2850, close 2723.15, range 191.94, upper tail 126.75, immediately after the two-bar bull spike of bars 77-78 (2507.15 to 2643.52).", "Rally from the bar-60 low 2358.62 to the bar-94 high 2850 = +491.38 (+20.8%) in 34 bars; pullback 2850 to 2633.31 (bar 112 low) = 216.69 (7.6%), about 44% of that leg.", "The last 26 bars are two-sided: bars 95-106 stayed inside 2716.01-2804.59 and bars 108-120 inside 2633.31-2740.42, with bar 107 (open 2726.71, close 2659.00) breaking the upper range to the downside.", "Final six bar ranges are 19.76, 25.65, 16.52, 69.24, 52.08, 17.82, and closes 2686.59/2677.28/2671.19/2715.90/2685.10/2692.59 overlap prior bars' ranges - numerous inside bars inside 2633.31-2740.42.", "Bars 1-33 traded two-sided between 2411.04 (bar 29 low) and 2528.80 (bar 8 high); bar 35 spiked to 2680.00 but closed at 2555.52, and bars 59-60 undercut to 2390.73 then 2358.62."], "phase": "range", "primary_regime": "bull-trend", "role": "CONTEXT_ANALYST", "schema": "brooks.market-context.v2", "structures": [{"description": "Opening 33 bars (1788638400000-1789099200000) form a two-sided range with upper 2528.80 (bar 8 high) and lower 2411.04 (bar 29 low); most closes stayed inside 2468-2513 with heavy bar overlap. The band was later exceeded upward by bar 35's spike to 2680.00 and undercut to 2390.73/2358.62 at bars 59-60.", "end_time_ms": 1789099200000, "kind": "range", "lower_boundary": "2411.04", "start_time_ms": 1788638400000, "upper_boundary": "2528.80"}, {"description": "Bull leg from the bar-60 low 2358.62 to the bar-94 high 2850, +491.38 (+20.8%) over 34 bars. Bars 77-78 were a 2495.82-2643.52 spike out of the prior range, bars 86-88 pulled back to 2568.16, and the leg ended with bar 94's 2658.81-2850 spike closing at 2723.15.", "end_time_ms": 1789977600000, "kind": "channel", "lower_boundary": "2358.62", "start_time_ms": 1789488000000, "upper_boundary": "2850"}, {"description": "Bar 94 (1789977600000, open 2658.81) ran to the window high 2850 and closed at 2723.15, leaving a 126.75 upper tail on a 191.94 range; the widest recent bar and a possible buy climax that began the current two-sided phase.", "end_time_ms": 1789977600000, "kind": "climax", "lower_boundary": null, "start_time_ms": 1789977600000, "upper_boundary": "2850"}, {"description": "Twelve-bar range at the highs: bars 95-106 held between 2716.01 (bar 99 low) and 2804.59 (bar 97 high), with repeated highs at 2748-2804 and lows at 2716-2737; bar 107 then closed at 2659.00 below the range low.", "end_time_ms": 1790150400000, "kind": "range", "lower_boundary": "2716.01", "start_time_ms": 1789992000000, "upper_boundary": "2804.59"}, {"description": "Current 13-bar two-sided range: bars 108-120 overlap inside 2633.31 (bar 112 low) and 2740.42 (bar 118 high), with repeated 2696.09-2699.53 highs; bar ranges shrank to 16.52-25.65 in bars 115-117 and 17.82 in bar 120, a tight range that is in breakout mode.", "end_time_ms": 1790352000000, "kind": "range", "lower_boundary": "2633.31", "start_time_ms": 1790179200000, "upper_boundary": "2740.42"}], "symbol": "ETH-USDT", "timeframe": "H4", "transition_conditions": ["Bull resolution: a close above 2804.59 with the next bar holding above it would reassert the bull trend toward and beyond 2850.", "Bear resolution: a close below 2633.31 that is not reversed, and then below 2568.16, would break the bull's higher-low sequence and shift the read from pullback to trading range/top.", "A close above 2740.42 (bar 118 high) with follow-through would be the first bull breakout from the current 13-bar range.", "Continued overlapping bars inside 2633.31-2740.42 keep the range phase and leave the structure a candidate bull flag until a boundary breaks."], "window_bars": 120}, "freshness": "current"}}, "raw": {"H1": [{"close": "2638.28", "close_time_ms": 1789945199999, "high": "2643.88", "low": "2627.79", "open": "2629.18", "open_time_ms": 1789941600000, "volume": "1769770.945"}, {"close": "2642.9", "close_time_ms": 1789948799999, "high": "2644.86", "low": "2631.42", "o